\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} 2D Filters}
\b\fs36\cf1 2D Filters
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This Tab allows you to apply 2-dimensional filter operations to the displayed image or the image store.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx5665\cellx10415\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \b 2D Filters\plain\fs24  Tab in the \b SEM Image Processing Control\plain\fs24  panel.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Source\plain\fs24  from the \ul Drop-down List\plain\fs24 {\v XYVXW3@Sem.HLP} (Buffer A = displayed image, Buffer B = stored image)
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Filter\plain\fs24  from the Drop-down List. See \uldb \b Filter Types\plain\b\fs24 {\v Filter_Types}\plain\fs24  for detail.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on \b Execute\plain\fs24  button to apply the filter to the image.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Undo\plain\fs24  button to cancel the previous filter application.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm1.bmp\} to \b close\plain\fs24  the control panel and leave the application.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Area Fraction Calculation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Area_Fraction_Calculation}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Area Fraction Calculation
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\}  \ul Clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Update\plain\fs24  button initiates an area fraction calculation.
\par 
\par The calculation is based on the \ul \b\ul detected area\plain\b\fs24 {\v Threshold_Range}\plain\fs24  defined by the Image Detect State and the Black and White thresholds.
\par 
\par The result  is displayed as a percentage of the image store area.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Black Level Detection}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Black_Level_Detection}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Area Fraction Calculation}
\b\fs36\cf1 Black Level Detection
\par \plain\fs24 Any pixel in the image store with a value less than the black threshold will be coloured RED.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Contents of Image Processing}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 2114YDN}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Contents of Image Processing
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The Image Processing option enables the contents of the image store to be manipulated using a \uldb \b Convolution Kernel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Convolution_Kernel>main}\plain\fs24 , addition and subtraction of images, detection of image levels, area fraction measurement, and histogram equalisation.
\par 
\par This option requires the \uldb \b Image Processing License\plain\b\fs24 {\v VDOITB@Sem.HLP}.\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm4.bmp\} The program is called from the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v 8ZP0K4@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  with menu \uldb \b Image\plain\b\fs24 {\v STFOS6@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  and sub menu \uldb \b Image Processing\plain\b\fs24 {\v 4MZO91S@Sem.HLP}
\par \pard 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\} \plain\fs24 Type \b <ALT + I> \plain\fs24 to open menu \ul I\plain\fs24 mage and then \b <P>\plain\fs24  to open the Image \ul P\plain\fs24 rocessing sub menu
\par 
\par The \b SEM Image Processing Control\plain\fs24  panel opens. 
\par 
\par Select from
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6235\cellx12685\pard\intbl \uldb \b 2D Filters\plain\b\fs24 {\v 2D_Filters>main}  \plain\fs24 applies 2-dimensional filter operations to the displayed image or the image store
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl \uldb \b Image Mathematics\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Mathematics>main} \plain\fs24 performs arithmetical operations on the displayed image and the image store\cell\intbl\row
\trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6235\cellx12685\pard\intbl \uldb \b Threshold\plain\b\fs24 {\v Threshold>main} \plain\fs24 allows you to highlight a range of pixel grey scale values in the image being displayed and to determine the area fraction of the range.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \uldb \b Histogram Equalisation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Histogram_Equalisation>main} \plain\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 to equalise the image store histogram
\par\intbl \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab to equalise the Look Up Table histogram
\par\intbl \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab to reset the Look Up Table\b \cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \page
