\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Design a Filter
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par A panel to enter the  \uldb \b Convolution Kernel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Convolution_Kernel}\plain\fs24  is opened.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx10705\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Enter a name in the \b Filter Name\plain\fs24  input box.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Enter the coefficients into the \b Filter Kernel Matrix \plain\fs24 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Enter the \b Division Factor\plain\fs24  as a scaling factor
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 The example shows a 3 x 3 averaging kernel.\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b OK\plain\fs24  button to enter the filter into the filter list.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Cancel \plain\fs24 button or close the panel with \{bmc bm1.bmp\} to break the action OFF without changing anything.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Help\plain\fs24  to display this help.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl See also \uldb \b User Defined Filter\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Defined_Filter}\plain\fs24 \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm16.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
