{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Histogram Equalisation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 13JON9P}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Histogram Equalisation
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The histogram equalisation uses the contents of the image store to calculate a \ul Look Up Table\plain\fs24 {\v 1QUPBH3@Sem.HLP} to transform the image to stretch the contrast of the image.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx5665\cellx10415\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select the \b Histogram Equalisation\plain\fs24  Tab in the \b SEM Image Processing Control\plain\fs24  panel.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on \uldb \b Histogram Equalisation Store\plain\b\fs24 {\v Histogram_Equalisation_Store}\plain\fs24  button to equalise the image store.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \uldb \b Histogram Equalisation LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v Histogram_Equalisation_LUT}\plain\fs24  button to equalise the output LUT.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on \b Reset LUT\plain\fs24  button to reset the LUT to standard values.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm1.bmp\} to \b close\plain\fs24  the control panel and leave the application.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm17.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
