\b\fs36\cf1 Image Maths Operations
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The operations consist of 
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \tab \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b Copy To\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Maths_Copy_To}:\plain\fs24  Copy image form Source to Destination
\par 
\par \tab \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b Exchange With\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Maths_Exchange_With}:\plain\fs24  Swap the Source and Destination images
\par 
\par \b \tab \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab \uldb Add\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Maths_Add}: \plain\fs24 Add the Source image to the Destination image and display the result
\par 
\par \b \tab \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab \uldb Subtract\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Maths_Subtract}: \plain\fs24 Subtract the Destination image from the Source image and display the result
\par 
\par \b \tab \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab \uldb Min\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Maths_Min}:\plain\fs24  Display the minimum value in either the Source or Destination image
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \b \tab \{bmc bm6.bmp\}\tab \uldb Max\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Maths_Max}: \plain\fs24 Display the maximum value in either the Source or Destination image
\par 
\par If one of the buffers contains no image the warning 
\par 
\par \tab \{bmc bm20.bmp\}
\par pops up.
